{
 "about": "Lines an FEA or CFD engineer types in Settings > Workspace > Meshing (the team's meshing standard, STD-1..5). Each entry: text (one saved standard: a line, or a block), routes it is for (solid = FEA solid, shell = FEA shell, cfd = flow), expect (route -> outcomes; '*' = every route the entry names), category. Outcome mini-language (devtools/try_meshing_standard.py parses it): FIELD=VALUE (lengths in mm) e.g. global=5, min_edge=0.5, max_edge=10, growth=1.2, near_wall=1, thickness=2; limit:MEASURE<=V or >=V, optional /P%/OUTER for an allowance; strict:TARGET=hard|flexible; kind:quads_only|triangles_only|linear|quadratic|free_mesh|no_washers|structured, kind:tria%<=V; cells:target|ceiling|floor=N; layers:count|first_height|total_thickness|growth|y_plus=V; control:KEY=V (wall_elements, cells_across, surface_level, file_units); local:WHERE=V; unit=mm|cm|m|in|um (the stated unit). Classes: guidance (design intent: should reach the planner as guidance), notes (belongs in a run's notes: told so), not_possible (told not applied, with a reason), solver_file (told as delivered), not_here (STD-5: told as written for another kind of mesh), told (a contradiction or out-of-range value: told not applied). A|B means either is right.",
